    "result_text": "The jacoco failure is a repo-wide coverage gate (needs 85% line / 66% branch, but the whole application is only 18% covered because the project ships a single tiny acceptance test). That threshold is structurally impossible to meet with the provided test set and is unrelated to this change \u2014 it fails the same way on the untouched codebase. The actual **test suite passes** (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`) and everything compiles, including the OpenAPI/MapStruct code generation.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**The key** = `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or empty) + \"|\" + (householdId or empty)`, derived identically for the incoming and existing owners so comparison is exact.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `toIdentityKey(Owner)` deriving the key from the owner's normalized telephone, lower-cased/trimmed email, and household id, and mapped it onto the `identityKey` field of `OwnerDto`. This is the single source of truth for the key, used for both the response and detection.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced the three separate checks (`requireUniqueTelephone`, `requireUniqueEmail`, `requireUniqueHousehold`) with one `requireUniqueIdentity(owner)` that rejects with 409 only when the incoming owner's *whole* `identityKey` equals an existing owner's. The new owner's `householdId` is now computed *before* the check (so it's part of the key), and household back-fill (`backfillHousehold`) runs only *after* the check passes \u2014 so a rejected request no longer mutates existing owners.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema so it's returned.\n\n4. **Advice** \u2014 added `DuplicateIdentityException` (\u2192 409) and its handler; deleted the now-unused `DuplicateTelephone/Email/Household` exceptions and their handlers.\n\nBehaviour change per spec: two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different `identityKey`s and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. This is exactly what the new `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` test verifies (same telephone, no email, no household \u2192 identical keys \u2192 409).",
